course: dictionary
lesson: 469
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Arrangement is one of these words. It can mean a plan, an agreement, a way things are put in order, or a version of a piece of music.
explain: «The teachers made arrangements for the school trip to the museum.» Arrangements here are plans made in advance. Ask yourself: what is being made? A trip needs plans, so the meaning fits.
explain: «We have an arrangement: I feed the cat and you walk the dog.» Here an arrangement is an agreement between people. Swap in the word agreement and see if the sentence still makes sense. It does, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: In maths, an arrangement is one possible order of a set of things. The letters A, B and C can be put in different orders, and each order is one arrangement. Counting them is a fun puzzle to try.
fact: An arrangement can be a plan, an agreement, a way of putting things in order, or a version of a piece of music.
fact: «Make arrangements» means to plan ahead, as in «make arrangements for a party».
fact: «By arrangement» means only if you have agreed a time first.
fact: In maths, arrangements are different orders of objects, like the letters A, B and C.
fact: Custody, or "arrangements", means deciding where children live and when they see each parent. A trained helper called a mediator can help parents reach an agreement.
exercise: «The teachers made arrangements for the school trip to the museum.» What does arrangements mean here? | *Plans made in advance | Loud noises | Paintings on the wall | Piles of wood
exercise: «We have an arrangement: I feed the cat and you walk the dog.» What is an arrangement here? | *An agreement between people | A fast race | A broken toy | A drawing of a cat
exercise: The letters A, B and C can be put in different orders. How many arrangements of the three letters are there? | 12 | 3 | *6 | 9
test: «The flowers in the vase were in a lovely arrangement.» What does arrangement mean here? | A long journey by train | A type of music played very loudly | *The way things are put in order | A lost ticket
test: «The shop is open to visitors by arrangement.» What does by arrangement mean? | Open all night | Closed forever | *Only if you have agreed a time first | Free for everyone
exam: «The band played a new arrangement of an old song for guitar and drums.» What is an arrangement of music? | A list of the band's members | A song with no tune | A loud, sudden noise | *A version of a piece written for certain instruments
